 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Right now, **parts of the Greater Johor Bahru area (specifically Pasir Gudang) are experiencing slightly worse 24-hour haze averages than Singapore**, though overall, both sides of the Causeway are enduring very similar **\"Unhealthy\"** air quality conditions.\n\n*(Note: Both Malaysia's Air Pollutant Index [API] and Singapore's Pollutant Standards Index [PSI] use the exact same scale for 24-hour rolling averages: **101–200 is Unhealthy**, and **201–300 is Very Unhealthy**).*\n\n### **Johor Bahru (DOE / APIMS Data)**\n* **Pasir Gudang (Eastern JB):** **196 API** *(Unhealthy — currently the highest reading in Malaysia, hovering just below the \"Very Unhealthy\" threshold after hitting 202 yesterday).*\n* **Larkin (Central JB):** **177 API** *(Unhealthy — eased slightly from 202 yesterday).*\n* **Surrounding Johor areas:** Kota Tinggi is at **172 API** and Pengerang is at **174 API**.\n\n### **Singapore (NEA Data)**\n* **24-Hour PSI:** Ranges from **139 to 184** across the island *(Unhealthy)*.\n  * **Central Singapore:** **184 PSI** *(Highest in Singapore, down from yesterday's \"Very Unhealthy\" peak of 229).*\n  * **Western Singapore:** **176 PSI**.\n* **1-Hour PM2.5 (Immediate Air Quality):** While overnight rain and shifting winds helped lower the 24-hour PSI averages, **hourly PM2.5 in Western Singapore spiked to 158 µg/m³ (\"High\" band)** around late morning, while the rest of the island remains between **83 and 144 µg/m³ (\"Elevated\" band)**.\n\n### **The Takeaway**\n* **On a 24-hour average:** **Pasir Gudang (196)** is worse than anywhere in Singapore right now. However, **Central JB / Larkin (177)** is actually slightly better off than **Central Singapore (184)** and essentially tied with **Western Singapore (176)**.\n* **Immediate conditions:** Because Western Singapore is seeing an active spike in 1-hour PM2.5 concentrations, the immediate air quality on the western side of the island (near Tuas) may feel just as bad or worse than central Johor Bahru. \n\nIf you are traveling between the two or spending time outdoors in either city today, health authorities on both sides are advising the public to minimize prolonged outdoor exertion and keep N95 masks handy, especially for vulnerable individuals.",
